(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mSummary:[70X
   A buffer is the in-memory text of a file.[5;4HA (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m is a viewport on a buffer.
   A tabpage is a collection of (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27ms.[5X
[43X
A (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m is a viewport onto a buffer.  You can use multiple (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27ms on one
buffer, or several (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27ms on different buffers.
[69X
A buffer is a file loaded into memory for editing.  The original file remains
unchanged until you write the buffer to the file.[6X

A buffer can be in one of three states:[39X
[13X[16;57H(B[0;1m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m]8;id=3790209051;https://neovim.io/doc/user/helptag/?tag=active-buffer\active-buffer]8;;\
(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27mactive:   The buffer is displayed in a (B[m[38;2;238;241;248m[48;2;107;83;0mwindow(B[m[38;2;224;226;234m[48;2;20;22;27m.  If there is a file for this
          buffer, it has been read into the buffer.  The buffer may have been
          modified since then and thus be different from the file.
